title remember_git_nib red caught by the cold run and closed with the follow-up shape
prompt The baton's rite: round-open, read the claim board, hold still through a cold endurance run, build, send, log.
think Read recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md whole, per the outer prompt's instruction to live inside it at the top of every lap.
think Ran fleet_round_open.sh -- clean at b293efaf35, thirteen dead-letter files noted (parked work, fold shelves, moved), nothing to act on this lap.
think Checked the claim board with fleet_claim_scan.sh -- five live claims, all past their six-hour expiry, verdict=clear.
think Confirmed no cold run already in flight with fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run -- both matches were this session's own prompt prose and process, refused _prose and _self.
think Read HEAD once (b293efaf35) and launched the cold run with --cadence-slice 1 per the baton's ORDER clause, then held fully still across six Monitor re-arms (~70 minutes) until the transcript carried run_verdict=.
think Cold run closed guard_red, 370 green, 9 red, 3 gated, tree_moved=no. Eight of the nine reds matched the standing set exactly; the ninth, new, was remember_git_nib.
think Investigated: the card named 9a338a4b8d, which by the time the guard ran was HEAD's grandparent rather than HEAD, its pre-amend sibling, or its parent. The prior lap's own commit b293efaf3 was a pure log-only follow-up (recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md edits, a new archive shelf, a session log, an index row) that touched nothing under construction/, so remember-git-nib.md rule 5 -- any commit landing beside the work commit carries the nib forward too -- went unapplied.
think Ran tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish bare, which named both candidate shapes (amend -> HEAD's parent c99fa8ee47; follow-up -> HEAD b293efaf35). Chose follow-up, since this lap was about to make a fresh work commit rather than amend one, and wrote HEAD as the card's nib so this commit's parent resolves once made. remember_git_nib_witness.rish read GREEN afterward (state=head, since the commit had not yet landed).
think Booked a fresh REDS row for the fault. Adding it pushed construction/REDS.md past its 65,536-byte bound with all sixteen numbered rows still OPEN and unfoldable by the automated tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh (which matches only a `**REDS %N ` prefix). Mirrored the precedent this exact class already set (REDS %735, and this same day's earlier c99fa8ee4 commit): hand-folded one closed, stamp-cited row (20260917.194613, the bare-tail-drops-header fix) onto a fresh shelf under construction/archive/REDS/, following the tool's own shape, and appended the recital line.
think Re-ran reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh (pin_headroom=1749, verdict=ok), reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish (GREEN, unchanged), and reds_shelf_resolve_scan.sh (verdict=ok, unchanged) to confirm the hand-fold left the ledger's own guards agreeing.
think Computed the council rota: commit count 6810, N mod 5 = 0, row 0 Aether -- hears. Read foundations/20260826-021731_aether-the-row-that-hears.md. Its teaching -- purpose is heard before motion is felt, and a lap that opens here asks what the work is FOR before what it touches -- fits this lap directly: the fix restores the card's own claim about which round it describes, rather than moving any code.
think Wrote this lap's account into recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md's next section (24,441 of 24,576 bytes, no shed needed this pass) and graded the REDS.md prose with qa_report_card.sh (B, composite 80, stands).
think Verified ASCII cleanliness on all three touched/created files with a raw byte grep and the ascii_document_scan.sh ratchet -- both clean, nothing flagged.
obs This is the second lap in a row to catch a genuine defect in the seam this fleet leans on hardest -- remember-git-nib is the tool that keeps the operator card honest about which commit it describes, and REDS %803 already closed half of it (the tool's two named shapes). This lap is evidence the remaining gap is a habit gap rather than a tool gap: the tool existed and named the right shape the moment it was asked, the missing step was asking at all after a log-only commit.
obs Chose to book a REDS row rather than treat this as routine confirmation, since a rostered guard answering red on metal for a reason distinct from the standing eight is exactly what reds-first asks to be named and recorded, even though the repair itself is one command.
rota lap 6810, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; its teaching (purpose before motion) matched the fix directly, since the repair concerns what the card CLAIMS about itself rather than any code path.
